      "GST registration basics every transporter must know. Transporters with annual turnover exceeding ₹40 lakh (₹20 lakh for special category states) must register for GST. Unregistered transporters cannot issue GSTIN invoices, limiting their ability to service registered businesses who need input tax credit on freight charges. Key filing deadlines: GSTR-1 (outward supplies) by the 11th, GSTR-3B (summary return) by the 20th, and annual GSTR-9. One important limitation: Input Tax Credit on fuel (petrol and diesel) is NOT available for GST-registered transporters. The GST paid on fuel purchases cannot be offset against GST collected on freight charges. However, ITC is available on vehicle purchases, spare parts, tyres, and maintenance services.",
      "Action Checklist: What Logistics Operators Should Do While the Rules Are Pending. Audit your ERP software so Ship-To GSTIN fields can be enabled quickly if the rule is re-notified, train drivers and field staff on standard e-Way Bill documentation, automate proof-of-delivery tracking, monitor your credit score, and leverage MSME support tools.",
