      "Earnings Comparison: With vs Without Return Load. A Ranchi to Kolkata one-way trip generates 25,000-35,000 rupees. Costs for the 420 km trip: diesel 10,000, tolls 3,500, maintenance 2,000, driver 1,500, misc 1,000. Total cost 18,000. Net profit without return: 7,000-17,000. With a return load (Kolkata to Ranchi, 25,000-30,000 revenue), round-trip revenue jumps to 50,000-65,000 and net profit to 32,000-47,000. That is a 15,000-30,000 difference per trip.",
      "Cargo Types Moving Out of Ranchi. Ranchi exports mining equipment, heavy machinery, agricultural produce (rice, wheat, pulses), and construction materials. The most common return-load cargo on Ranchi corridors includes steel products from Jamshedpur, textiles and FMCG from Kolkata, agricultural goods from Bhubaneswar, and coal-related equipment from Dhanbad. Each corridor has distinct cargo characteristics that affect loading requirements and vehicle type.",
